   "daf": "25b",
   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "בִּרְכַּת כֹּהֲנִים נִקְרִין וְלֹא מִתַּרְגְּמִין. מַאי טַעְמָא? מִשּׁוּם דִּכְתִיב: ״יִשָּׂא״.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: The verses constituting «the Priestly Benediction [birkat kohanim]» are «read but not translated.» The Gemara asks: «What is the reason» for this? The Gemara explains that it is «because it is written:» “May the Lord «lift up» His countenance to you” (Numbers 6:26). Listeners may understand this to mean that God shows unfair favoritism to the Jewish people."
  }
